From 8fcd8d906a78548fae749a800a3e7f805e7f233d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:34:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] avoid pooling pins for published checkout-only
 deletions

The owning clone in worker-a1 t_eeeeee0000000034 had 22,692 staged D-space deletions and an empty index, not the initially reported unstaged space-D pattern (card evidence comment 18532). HEAD was contained in its upstream; its real published PR worktree was clean. A generic dirty verdict pinned the pooled card to one worker.

Recognize only uniform unstaged deletions, or uniform staged deletions with an empty index. Require a symbolic branch with upstream containing HEAD, no hidden index edits, hardened Git probes and the existing shared deadline. Mixed edits, partial staged deletion, missing upstream, local commits and unknown checks still pin. Keep child scanning and removal dirty checks unchanged.

Proof: RED four acceptance cases on main, GREEN 26 focused tests; all 24 move/park/unpin consumers and subprocess guard files pass (2067 tests). Five safety-condition mutants killed; scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks OK.
